attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 3, `hemB` to `tauB`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2 to 5% of calls {S1}. The model names 94 to 98% of them, fewest at column 1, `tauD`, 94% {S1}.

@variable **A fork and variable stretch follows**, columns 4 to 8, carried by 60 to 90%, [[taurine transport]] {S2, Q}. Then the `mhp` genes, columns 13 to 20, [[hydroxyphenylpropionate catabolism]], carried by 83 to 86% {S4, Q}. Through columns 41 to 45 a branch of 5 families runs in 21 to 22%, [[ABC transport]] {S8.b41, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.29 against 0.69 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 6, `yaiP`, a fork column, 1.55 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 56 to 79 are carried by 13 to 88%, 23 shell and 1 persistent {S10}. The last column is `paoB`, in 35% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 89% of genes**, 0.58 bits on average, perplexity 1.9 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.69 against 0.26 bits, and names fewer genes, 87% against 95% {C}.

